  "description": "A chain of storm-scoured island nations is locked in the Long Reckoning, a Napoleonic-inspired war between the Verrane Maritime Republic and the Auric Dominion. It is fought by great fleets under sail, with no explosive powder anywhere. Ships are armed with torsion ballistae, tar-fire projectors and ramming prows. Sea law is kept in the Corsair's Code, a written covenant of honor that binds even privateers, and the war is as much about who may legally claim a sea lane as about who wins a battle. The tone is stoic. Duty is carried quietly, grief is rationed, and officers speak little and mean all of it. At the center is a naval officer of the Republic who learns that the Dominion's admiral is the brother he has not spoken to in twenty years. The two were raised under one oath in the same drowned harbor town, and the Code now forces each to weigh blood against allegiance.",
